# Frequent collectors — hourly weather, 6h maritime/portugal
# Weather hourly for storm freshness (AEMET alerts change within minutes)
0 * * * * TASK=weather npx tsx index.ts 2>&1 && touch /tmp/last-run
# ESCALONADOS A PROPOSITO (21-09-2026). Los dos iban a `0 */6`, el mismo minuto en
# que ya arrancan `weather` y `voyage-detector` (los dos a :00): CUATRO procesos de
# node a la vez, con 700 MB de heap cada uno, en un contenedor de 1 GB. El kernel
# mataba a uno en cada tanda -- oom-kill a las 00:00:18, 06:00:19, 18:00 (x2)... -- y
# la victima rotaba: un dia voyage-detector ("previous run still in progress"), otro
# portugal-weather, otro maritime-forecast. Nadie lo arreglaba porque el health-check
# de collector-realtime relanza lo caducado a las dos horas y tapa el sintoma.
# Minutos ocupados en este tier: :00 weather+voyage · :20 flight · :35 train.
10 */6 * * * TASK=maritime-forecast npx tsx index.ts 2>&1
45 */6 * * * TASK=portugal-weather npx tsx index.ts 2>&1
# NOTE: air-quality runs in the realtime crontab (hourly at :00) — do NOT add here

# Voyage detector — groups VesselPosition rows into PortCalls & Voyages (hourly)
# Idempotent upsert; requires AIS positions to be flowing (ais-stream container)
# Lockfile guard: skip if a previous run is still in progress (takes 2-4h for 55k vessels)
0 * * * * flock -n /tmp/voyage-detector.lock -c 'TASK=voyage-detector npx tsx index.ts 2>&1' || echo "[voyage-detector] skipped — previous run still in progress"

# SASEMAR: historical archive (2019-2024), one-shot only — do NOT re-enable on cron
# SASEMAR maritime emergencies — historical ArcGIS upsert (every 15 min)
# Source: opendata-sasemar.hub.arcgis.com (2019-2024 historical records)
# Idempotent: upserts by external ID; safe to run frequently
#*/15 * * * * TASK=sasemar npx tsx index.ts 2>&1

# Derive permanent per-airframe flight history from 7-day raw positions
20 * * * * flock -n /tmp/flight-detector.lock -c 'TASK=flight-detector npx tsx index.ts 2>&1' || echo "[flight-detector] skipped — previous run still in progress"

# Derive permanent per-train service history from the 48h position window
35 * * * * flock -n /tmp/train-service-detector.lock -c 'TASK=train-service-detector npx tsx index.ts 2>&1' || echo "[train-service-detector] skipped — previous run still in progress"
